# SocietyEats

SocietyEats is the product. The repo and `societybites-backend` still use the SocietyBites name. Read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/LATEST_HANDOVER.md` before editing.

- Inspect the existing route, `societybites-backend/lib` module, Prisma model, and Flutter screen. Extend them.
- Keep the diff limited to the request. Do not refactor unrelated code.
- Preserve uncommitted work and stashes. Do not commit or push unless the owner asks.
- The code overrides `docs/01`–`docs/17` and the local pickup-only skill when they disagree. Delivery, selling reach, and saved places are already in the product.
- Do not add a payment vendor, WhatsApp vendor, or host without approval. Direct UPI stays the default.
- WhatsApp and FCM failures must not fail orders.
- Identity comes from the JWT on the server.
- Never write secrets into source, docs, or chat.
- Do not claim tests passed unless you ran them.
- After a significant change, update `docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md` and `docs/LATEST_HANDOVER.md`, plus any architecture, schema, API, decision, issue, or roadmap page the change affects.
- Flutter screens stay Flutter-specific. On a wide Chrome window, center content in the existing web frame (`webFrameMaxWidth` 1180, seller tools 840). Do not stretch phone layouts, cards, forms, or switches to the browser edges, and do not show a stretched desktop mockup.
